  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n```html\n<script>\nlet w = window.open(\"javascript:null\");\nw.onload = () => console.log('w: got load event');\n</script>\n```\n\nIn Chrome, this prints a load event. In Firefox and Safari it does not. My read of the spec agrees with Firefox and Safari:\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#the-javascript:-url-special-case - step 8 returns\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#beginning-navigation:navigate-to-a-javascript:-url - step 21 queues the task and does nothing else\n\nI don't have a sense for what is the right direction to get alignment between browsers, however.",
